				155,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Standardize IPC method naming and add webview option bridge\n\nUpdate IPC method identifiers in `InstallEditorAndOutput.ts` to use the new lowercase `file:` namespace (`file:writeFile`, `file:rename`, `file:delete`) instead of the previous `FileSystem.` prefix. This aligns the bridge layer with the updated Mountain backend protocol conventions.\n\nIn `InstallWebview.ts`, implement the `sky://webview/setOptions` bridge listener to handle runtime configuration updates (e.g., `enableScripts`, `localResourceRoots`). The handler resolves the target webview panel from the global registry and invokes the native `setOptions` method, supporting both Cocoon-originated requests and direct notifications.\n\nThese changes streamline the IPC contract and ensure webview lifecycle operations are handled synchronously and deterministically within the Sky component layer.",
			"SHA": "faa9c2543f6c806b9af5ef86198469a660b4e7d1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:25:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Distinguish custom URI stringification from default Object methods\n\nUpdate the URI reconstruction logic in `InstallScm.ts` to safely parse string representations of URI objects. The previous check `typeof UriField.toString === \"function\"` was insufficient as it returned true for the default `Object.prototype.toString`, causing non-URI objects to be incorrectly passed to `Services.URI.parse`.\n\nAdd an explicit check ensuring `UriField.toString` is not the inherited default method. This prevents false positives during Source Control Manager bridge operations where generic objects might erroneously trigger URI parsing, ensuring only legitimate URI instances with custom stringification are processed.\n\nThis aligns with the recent refactoring of bridge layers to remove retry loops, requiring deterministic and accurate type handling during immediate service execution.",
			"SHA": "7f22e3facc226ce9809831cf28a73e43ddf703eb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:19:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Invalidate build cache when manifest count is zero\n\nAdjust the `BakeExtensionManifest` build logic to treat an empty extension cache as a stale state. Previously, the build system relied solely on file modification times, which caused hangs if a cached manifest recorded zero extensions but the binary bundle still existed.\n\nRetrieve the cached manifest content and parse its `count` field. If the count is missing or zero, flag the cache as a stub. Modify the `AnyNewer` check to invalidate the cache when `CacheStub` is true, forcing a regeneration of the manifest rather than using a stale empty record.\n\nThis prevents the build process from incorrectly skipping regeneration when no extensions are present, ensuring the live extension host receives accurate metadata and falls back to runtime scanning as intended.",
			"SHA": "0d44e5000fc6ce302b3ab76f36d70aeab0dd3b7a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:17:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Eliminate retry loops and forced UI state in diagnostics and tree view bridges\n\nRemove aggressive retry mechanisms and forced panel manipulation from `InstallDiagnostics.ts` and `InstallTreeView.ts` to align with the stabilized workbench bootstrap sequence.\n\nIn `InstallDiagnostics`, delete the logic that forced the Problems panel open or cleared the `activeFile` filter upon diagnostic arrival. The bridge now strictly reacts to `IMarkerService` changes without assuming or manipulating visibility, relying on the `MarkersView` to handle state naturally.\n\nIn `InstallTreeView`, strip out the exponential backoff retry logic, pending attach queues, and delayed hook installation. The `AttachDataProvider` now executes synchronously; if the `TreeView` service is unavailable, the registration fails immediately rather than entering a polling loop. This assumes the workbench services are ready when bridge functions are invoked.\n\nThese changes reduce bundle size, eliminate hidden asynchronous delays, and remove complex error-handling paths that previously masked upstream initialization timing issues.\n\nCloses: Aligns with previous simplification of extension bridge layers.",
			"SHA": "14346f54c84b5c160190b4af3340e78dec9e7601"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:12:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Remove aggressive retry logic from extension bridge layers\n\nEliminate complex retry mechanisms and polling loops across multiple bridge installation modules that were previously used to compensate for workbench service initialization race conditions. In InstallInlineCompletions, InstallScm, InstallSearch, and InstallTreeView, replace exponential backoff and event-listener rescue paths with direct service acquisition and synchronous execution.\n\nThe previous implementations guarded against early-arriving IPC events by deferring registration or re-attempting connection until specific services (LanguageFeatures, SCM, Search, TreeView) became available. This approach introduced significant code complexity, unbounded execution paths, and potential resource leaks.\n\nThis change assumes the workbench bootstrap sequence has been stabilized elsewhere, allowing the bridge layers to execute registration logic immediately upon invocation. Failed registrations now fail fast and silently rather than entering retry cycles, aligning with the architecture's expectation that service availability is guaranteed by the time bridge installation functions are called.\n\nThe simplification reduces bundle size, removes hidden asynchronous delays in feature activation, and makes the bridge logic strictly deterministic and easier to reason about.",
			"SHA": "9c424d95afa5fdc1f65032b0835eeb557289f8dd"
		}
	],
